From: sheng-development
Subject: [PATCH] Signal a geometry change when the screen rotates

ScreenModel re-reads the screen on every data() call but never tells anyone
the geometry changed, and a rotation keeps the same QScreen. The greeter's
window is resized by the compositor, so a theme that anchors to it follows
along, but a binding on the model's geometry role does not: in Breeze that is
the per-screen wallpaper, which keeps drawing at the size the screen had when
the greeter started.

--- a/src/greeter/ScreenModel.cpp
+++ b/src/greeter/ScreenModel.cpp
@@ -32,6 +32,11 @@ namespace SDDM {
 
     ScreenModel::ScreenModel(QScreen *screen, QObject *parent) : QAbstractListModel(parent), d(new ScreenModelPrivate()) {
         d->screen = screen;
+
+        connect(screen, &QScreen::geometryChanged, this, [this] {
+            const QModelIndex row = index(0, 0);
+            emit dataChanged(row, row, { GeometryRole });
+        });
     }
 
     ScreenModel::~ScreenModel() {
